# {{ProjectName}}

Open `{{ProjectName}}.hertaproject` with HertaEditor. The Game template includes an empty level and a native C++ module, not a standalone game runtime.

Generate projects from the associated Herta source checkout with its pinned Premake:

`premake5 --file=<engine>/premake5.lua --project=<project>/{{ProjectName}}.hertaproject vs2026`

On Linux use `gmake`. Build the `{{ModuleName}}` static library in the generated workspace. Build rules stay in the engine; project descriptors and templates never execute build scripts.
